# Observability & Monitoring

## Logging
- Prefer structured JSON logging
- Include correlation IDs (trace_id, span_id)
- Assume logs ship to Loki, traces to Tempo/OTel, metrics to Prometheus/OTel
- Avoid tool lock-in

## Performance Monitoring
- For async or performance-sensitive code, suggest profiling hooks
- Use py-spy, pyinstrument, cProfile and tracemalloc for memory analysis

## KQL & Data
- Keep KQL artefacts (functions, tables, mappings) idempotent and foldered properly
- Prefer `.create-or-alter` for KQL operations
- For ingestion mappings, validate JSON schemas
- Avoid breaking changes—use versioned mappings when needed
- For monitoring notebooks/jobs, emit structured events with stable keys